eBPF Mesh is licensed per directory:

  ebpf/, tests/common/, tests/bpf/
      GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause (SPDX: GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
      The BPF program must be GPL-compatible to use GPL-only kernel helpers
      (e.g. the SYN-cookie helpers in Phase 1); the BSD option keeps the ABI
      headers usable from non-GPL code.

  everything else (userspace/, tests/integration/, scripts/, lab/, docs/, ...)
      MIT OR Apache-2.0 (SPDX: MIT OR Apache-2.0)

Full texts: LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt, LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt,
LICENSES/MIT.txt, LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. C sources carry an
SPDX-License-Identifier; Rust crates declare theirs in Cargo.toml.
